# Normalise line endings: the repository stores LF, and checkouts are LF on
# every platform.
#
# Why this exists: with core.autocrlf=true (the Git for Windows default) and no
# .gitattributes, a Windows checkout silently rewrites LF to CRLF in the working
# copy while the repository still stores LF. Committed content is unaffected, but
# any byte-level check - SHA-256, file size, a diff against an upstream original
# - then reports differences that do not exist in the repository. That happened
# once, during a byte-for-byte check of LICENSE against the canonical Apache
# text, and produced a 202-byte phantom difference.
#
# Every file in this repository is text; there is nothing here for which a
# platform-native checkout would be preferable.
* text=auto eol=lf
